       <div class="col-lg-8">
             <!-- Blog Main Content Here -->
             <!-- Use class 'blog-content' for the wrapper -->
             <!-- CRITICAL: The main image MUST have src="data:image/jpeg;base64," -->
             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="NEET Admit Card 2026">
             <div class="blog-content">
                <div class="blog-body">
                    <h1 class="blog-title text-center mb-4">NEET Admit Card 2026: Your Essential Guide to the Medical Entrance Exam</h1>
                    <p>The National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET UG) is the single largest medical entrance examination in India, a crucial stepping stone for aspiring doctors seeking admission to MBBS, BDS, AYUSH, and veterinary courses across the nation. With approximately 26 lakh students registered this year, the competition is intense, and staying informed about vital updates, especially regarding the NEET Admit Card 2026, is paramount. The National Testing Agency (NTA) is the organizing body responsible for conducting NEET UG, and they have already released the official notification and key dates for NEET UG 2026.</p>

                    <div class="section-title">Key Dates for NEET UG 2026</div>
                    <p>Understanding the complete timeline for NEET UG 2026 is crucial for every aspirant. Here’s a summary of the important dates:</p>
                    <table>
                        <thead>
                            <tr>
                                <th>Event</th>
                                <th>Date</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td>NEET 2026 Official Notification Release</td>
                                <td>February 8, 2026</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>NEET 2026 Application Start Date</td>
                                <td>February 8, 2026</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>NEET 2026 Application Last Date</td>
                                <td>March 11, 2026 (9:00 PM)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>NEET 2026 Fee Payment Last Date</td>
                                <td>March 11, 2026 (11:50 PM)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>NEET 2026 Application Correction Window</td>
                                <td>March 12 - 14, 2026 (Closed)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>NEET 2026 City Intimation Slip Release</td>
                                <td>Mid-April 2026</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>NEET 2026 Admit Card Release</td>
                                <td>End of April 2026</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>NEET 2026 Exam Date</td>
                                <td>May 3, 2026 (Sunday, 2:00 PM - 5:00 PM)</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td>NEET 2026 Result Declaration (Anticipated)</td>
                                <td>Mid-June 2026</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>

                    <div class="section-title">NEET Admit Card 2026: Your Gateway to the Exam Hall</div>
                    <p>The NEET Admit Card is arguably the most critical document for candidates appearing for the examination. Without it, entry into the examination center is strictly prohibited. It serves as a comprehensive identification and examination pass, containing essential details about both the candidate and the examination.</p>

                    <h3 class="section-title">When to Expect Your Admit Card</h3>
                    <p>The NTA is expected to release the NEET Admit Card 2026 by the end of April 2026, typically three to four days before the scheduled exam date of May 3, 2026. Prior to the admit card, candidates will also receive a NEET UG city intimation slip in mid-April, which informs them about their allotted exam city.</p>

                    <h3 class="section-title">How to Download Your NEET 2026 Admit Card</h3>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official Website</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Navigate to the official NTA NEET website: <a href="https://neet.nta.nic.in/" target="_blank">neet.nta.nic.in</a>.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">2. Locate the Admit Card Link</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, look for and click on the "NEET UG 2026 Admit Card" login link.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">3. Enter Your Credentials</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">You will be prompted to enter your NEET application number, date of birth (or password), and a security pin.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">4. Download and Print</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">After successful submission, your NEET Admit Card 2026 will be displayed on the screen. Download it and take a printout. It is advisable to print multiple copies for safety.</div>
                    </div>

                    <h3 class="section-title">Details on Your Admit Card</h3>
                    <p>Ensure all the following details are correctly mentioned on your NEET Admit Card 2026:</p>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ Candidate's Name and Roll Number</p>
                        <p>✅ Application Number</p>
                        <p>✅ Photograph and Signature</p>
                        <p>✅ Exam Date and Timing (May 3, 2026, 2:00 PM - 5:00 PM)</p>
                        <p>✅ Full Address of the Allotted Exam Centre</p>
                        <p>✅ Important Exam-Day Instructions</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="highlight-text">
                        <p><strong>Critical Reminder:</strong> After downloading, candidates must paste a postcard-size photograph on their NEET Admit Card 2026, as this is a mandatory requirement for entry into the examination hall.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="section-title">Important Exam Day Guidelines</div>
                    <p>To ensure a smooth examination experience, pay close attention to the following guidelines:</p>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ Carry your NEET Admit Card 2026 with a pasted postcard-size photograph.</p>
                        <p>✅ Bring a valid photo ID proof (Aadhaar Card, PAN Card, Voter ID, etc.).</p>
                        <p>✅ Reach the exam centre well before the reporting time to avoid last-minute rush.</p>
                        <p>✅ Strictly adhere to the dress code specified by NTA.</p>
                        <p>✅ Do not carry any prohibited items such as electronic devices, study material, or any unauthorized accessories.</p>
                        <p>✅ Follow all instructions given by the invigilators.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="section-title">Troubleshooting Common Admit Card Issues</div>
                    <p>While the process is generally smooth, candidates might encounter issues. Here's what to do:</p>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">1. Discrepancies in Details</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">If you find any errors in your name, photograph, signature, or other details, immediately contact the NTA Helpdesk for rectification. Although the correction window has closed, critical errors might still be addressed by the authorities.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="benefit-item">
                        <div class="benefit-title">2. Unable to Download</div>
                        <div class="benefit-content">Ensure you have a stable internet connection and are using the correct application number and date of birth/password. If the issue persists, clear your browser cache or try again after some time. If problems continue, contact NTA support.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="section-title">NEET UG 2026 at a Glance</div>
                    <p>For those preparing, here’s a quick overview of the exam:</p>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                        <p>✅ **Mode of Exam:** Offline (Pen &amp; Paper Based)</p>
                        <p>✅ **Duration:** 180 Minutes (3 hours)</p>
                        <p>✅ **Total Questions:** 200 (180 to be attempted)</p>
                        <p>✅ **Subjects:** Physics, Chemistry, Botany, Zoology</p>
                        <p>✅ **Language:** 13 different languages available</p>
                        <p>✅ **Total Seats:** Over 1,00,000 MBBS, 27,618 BDS, 52,720 AYUSH, 603 BVSc &amp; AH, along with 1,899 AIIMS, and 249 JIPMER seats.</p>
                    </div>

                    <p>The NEET 2026 syllabus has been officially released by the UGMEB on the NMC's official website on December 22, 2025, providing clarity on the final syllabus to be followed for the upcoming exam.</p>

                    <div class="cta-section">
                        <h2>Stay Ahead of the Curve!</h2>
                        <p>Don't miss any critical updates for NEET UG 2026. Bookmark the official NTA NEET website and regularly check for announcements regarding admit cards, city intimation slips, and results.</p>
                        <a href="https://neet.nta.nic.in/" target="_blank" class="btn btn-light mt-3">Visit Official Website</a>
                    </div>

                    <p>With the NEET UG 2026 exam date set for May 3, 2026, consistent preparation and awareness of all logistical aspects, including the admit card release, are key to success. Ensure all your details are accurate, keep your admit card safe, and focus on your studies to achieve your dream of a career in medicine.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
       </div>

            
            
